# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: release-all-zip-appledouble-entries — the -all.zip ships macOS AppleDouble ._* files
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: infra
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-release-links-and-macos-metadata

* Context

Found while verifying the artefacts of =release-1.8.49= (the release that
moved the sources under =src/=). The layout check itself passed; this is a
separate defect the listing made visible.

* Problem

=clautolisp-1.8.49-all.zip= carries an AppleDouble sidecar next to every
top-level directory:

#+begin_example
$ unzip -Z1 clautolisp-1.8.49-all.zip | sed 's|/.*||' | sort -u
._.
._bin
._etc
._include
._lib
._libexec
._share
bin
etc
include
lib
libexec
share
src
#+end_example

The =.tar.bz2= union of the same tree is clean — it has exactly the eight
real top levels and nothing else — so this is specific to the zip
container.

=._NAME= files are how macOS stores extended attributes and resource forks
on filesystems that have none. They appear when a tree carrying macOS
xattrs is archived by a tool that preserves them. The darwin-arm64 lane's
artefacts are part of the union, which is the likely source.

* Why it matters

They are not merely cosmetic:

- on Linux and Windows they extract as visible junk beside every directory,
  so the first thing a user sees after unzipping a release is seven files
  that are not part of the product;
- they are not in the =tar.bz2=, so the two containers of the *same* union
  do not unpack to the same tree — the property a =-all= artefact exists to
  provide;
- =manifest-*.txt= does not list them, so the archive contains files the
  provenance manifest does not account for.

* Options

1. =zip -X= (or =--no-extra=) when building the union, which drops extra
   file attributes.
2. Strip the xattrs from the staged tree before archiving
   (=xattr -cr= on macOS, or exclude =._*= at archive time: =zip -x '._*' -x '*/._*'=).
3. Stop the darwin lane from producing them in the first place
   (=COPYFILE_DISABLE=1= in its packaging step).

Option 3 is the cleanest — it prevents them rather than deleting them
afterwards — but option 1 also protects against any future macOS-authored
input. Doing both is cheap.

* Verification

The check belongs with the layout assertion already in =release-sources=
and the =-all= recipes: after writing the zip, fail if any entry matches
=._*=. That turns this from a thing someone notices into a thing the build
refuses to ship, which is the pattern 1.8.47 and 1.8.49 established for
release artefacts.

* Resolution (2026-08-19, clautolisp 1.8.51)

Fixed at both ends, because the two ends fail differently.

*At the source.* =pack-release-artefact= now packs with
=COPYFILE_DISABLE=1=, =--exclude= on =._*= and =--no-xattrs=, so the
darwin artefact stops carrying macOS metadata at all. That also removes
the =LIBARCHIVE.xattr.com.apple.provenance= pax headers, which made GNU
tar print /Ignoring unknown extended header keyword/ 23 times on every
extraction of =clautolisp-1.8.49-binaries-darwin-arm64.tar.bz2=
elsewhere — the same defect in its quieter form, and the reason to fix
this at the source rather than only filter it later. =--no-xattrs= is
PROBED (=tar --no-xattrs --version=) rather than assumed: GNU tar and
bsdtar spell their options differently, and a tar that rejected the flag
would have taken the darwin release lane down with it. =COPYFILE_DISABLE=
and =--exclude= already do the visible half of the job on any tar.

*At the packaging.* The =-all.zip= and the per-target Windows =.zip= now
carry the same exclusion the tar branches always had — that asymmetry
was the whole bug. The recipe then RE-READS the zip it just wrote and
fails if any =._= entry survived.

* Verification

Both directions, which is the only thing that makes a guard worth having:

- =scripts/check-release-artefact-set.sh= now fabricates its darwin
  inputs *with* AppleDouble members, because the real ones have them: a
  check fed only clean input cannot tell an exclusion that works from one
  that was deleted. It then asserts that neither =-all= container carries
  any.
- removing the zip exclusion makes =collect-artefacts= itself abort:
  /ERROR: clautolisp-0.0.0-check-all.zip carries the macOS metadata file
  'marker/._binaries-darwin-arm64'/.
- removing the in-recipe assertion as well makes the script-level check
  fail instead: /FAIL: -all.zip carries macOS metadata that the union must
  drop/.

* Not done

The artefacts of 1.8.47 and 1.8.49 are not rebuilt: they are published
and immutable, and the junk is inert on extraction. The fix applies from
the next release on.
